    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class and it passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `salutation` feature by threading a new `title` field through the existing Owner request/response pipeline, reusing the established derived-field pattern rather than adding any new orchestration.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `title` field (`@Column(name = \"title\")`) with getter/setter, alongside the other owner columns.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `salutation` mapping following the exact convention of the existing derived fields (`displayName`, `initials`, etc.): a `@Mapping(target = \"salutation\", expression = \"java(salutation(owner))\")` plus a small `default String salutation(Owner owner)` that returns `title + \" \" + lastName`, or just `lastName` when no title is present.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `title` (optional string, values MR/MRS/MS/DR) to the editable `OwnerFields` schema, and `salutation` (readOnly) to the `Owner` response schema. These regenerate the `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` at build time; `title` auto-maps by name into the entity and `salutation` comes out via the mapper.\n\n4. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `title` column to the `owners` table (hsqldb is the profile the tests use, with `ddl-auto=none`; the others updated for consistency).\n\nNo YAML/function wiring changes were needed \u2014 `BuildOwner` and `RespondWithOwner` already round-trip through `OwnerMapper`, so the title flows in on create and the salutation flows out on GET automatically.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreComposesSalutation` (create owner with `title=DR`, `lastName=who` \u2192 `GET` returns `salutation = \"DR who\"`) passes, and the build is green.",
